  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#bidi-rendering\n\n> unicode-bidi:​ isolate; \n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-ruby/#default-stylesheet has\n\n```\nruby, rb, rt, rbc, rtc { unicode-bidi: isolate; }\n```\n\n(Of those only `ruby` and `rt` are conforming in HTML currently.)\n\nThis sort of makes sense to me, but I don't now how common ruby annotations mix LTR and RTL in practice.\n\ncc @fantasai\n",
